      'Start from the concerns, not the diagrams (R62 p.344). Three stakeholders ask three different questions of the same architecture. A vertiport operator (STK-005) asks how an arriving aircraft gets back into service. A system designer asks which transformations every trip needs, whoever performs them. The board and the investors (STK-003) ask what must be bought and connected. Each question defines a viewpoint, and the table shows the view the reference builds for it. The rows are consistent with each other: the operational view’s steps are realised by the functional view’s FNs, which are allocated to the physical view’s PHYs. MITRE’s advice to identify the information views share and to manage it centrally (R62 p.345) is what the IDs make possible.',
